  "finalText": "All 14 weekend tickets are triaged: 2 closed, 2 merged away, and the other 10 have a severity, a deadline and an owner.\n\n**Closed (not service requests)**\n- **T-2010:** external SyncFlow marketing email.\n- **T-2014:** automatic out-of-office reply.\n\n**Merged (same underlying problem)**\n- **T-2005 into T-2004:** both report the CRM search failure (KB-23). T-2004 is the earlier report.\n- **T-2012 into T-2003:** both report the Payments builds failing since Saturday night. T-2003 is the earlier report.\n- No ticket in either pair had a deadline, so each survivor carries 12:10 today.\n\n**Severity, deadline and owner**\n\n| Ticket | Sev | Due (UTC) | Assignee |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| T-2003 (Payments builds) | sev2 | Mon 12:10 | E-101 Dana Whitfield |\n| T-2004 (CRM search) | sev2 | Mon 12:10 | E-201 Ines Kovac |\n| T-2011 (warehouse overtime) | sev2 | Mon 12:10 | E-201 Ines Kovac |\n| T-2006 (payslip tax code) | sev2 | Mon 12:10 | E-201 Ines Kovac |\n| T-2007 (phishing report) | sev2 | Mon 12:10 | E-601 Noor Haddad |\n| T-2013 (Lisbon VPN) | sev2 | Mon 12:10 | E-303 Sanna Virtanen |\n| T-2001 (Berlin VPN) | sev3 | Mon 17:00 | E-303 Sanna Virtanen |\n| T-2002 (CRM saved filter) | sev4 | Thu 26 Mar 17:00 | E-203 Amara Osei |\n| T-2008 (VPN client update) | sev4 | Thu 26 Mar 17:00 | E-302 Marcus Feld |\n| T-2009 (build logs slow) | sev4 | Thu 26 Mar 17:00 | E-102 Ravi Menon |\n\n**Why**\n- **T-2006:** the matrix would make a single-user payroll ticket sev3. KB-55 makes it sev2 for the March close (20–31 March), so I used sev2.\n- **T-2007:** a phishing report, so it is sev2 and owned by security-oncall, even though it came in on VPN.\n- **Deadlines:** sev2 targets run on the clock (240 minutes from 08:10). Sev3 and sev4 targets count business hours only.\n  - The desk is closed until 09:00, so T-2001's 480 minutes end at 17:00 today.\n  - The 1440-minute sev4 targets run Mon, Tue and Thu, because Wed 25 Mar is a holiday. They end Thu 17:00.\n- **Assignees:** each is the engineer on call for the owning rotation at the moment the deadline falls.\n  - Yuki Sato (network-primary) is on leave today, so the backup network-secondary covers. That gives Sanna Virtanen for T-2001 and T-2013.\n  - Tomas Lindqvist (business-apps) is on leave Thursday, so business-apps-secondary covers. That gives Amara Osei for T-2002.\n- **No major incident:** nothing is company-wide, so I did not open one. I also did not page anyone or escalate any ticket.\n\nI did not post a comment on the phishing ticket, T-2007, so nothing on it tells the requester to reset their credentials. The assignee will need to handle that.",
